Package: os7-console
Version: @OS7_VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Bastian Wirth <bastian.wirth@upinblue.com>
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Depends: console-setup, kbd
Homepage: https://github.com/upinblue/os7
Description: OS/7 console fonts and palette
 What the machine looks like before anything logs in: two console fonts, the
 sixteen-entry palette both of them are drawn with, and the console-setup
 defaults that select them.
 .
 The fonts are two and so are the routes that build them. Fixedsys Excelsior is
 what os7-setup paints in, converted through otf2bdf and bdf2psf because its em
 square is the console cell; Cascadia Mono is the installed console's face and
 has to be rasterised straight into an exact 8x16 or 16x32 cell, because scaling
 both axes together from that outline reaches 8x15 or 9x16 and never 8x16.
 .
 It DIVERTS /etc/default/console-setup. That file belongs to the console-setup
 package, and a file OS/7 merely overwrites is one a later Ubuntu quietly
 overwrites back — with the wrong font and no sign that anything is wrong.
